    'terms.start': 'Start',
    'terms.termsBody': 'Effective 13 November 2026 · Version 1.0\n\n1. About these terms\nThese terms are an agreement between you ("User") and the developer quiteusefulapp ("Developer") about using the mobile app Smart Shopping List (also named "Умный список покупок" and "Smart Tizim"; the "App"). By installing or using the App you accept these terms. If you do not agree, do not install or use the App. How data is handled is described in the Privacy Policy.\n\n2. Licence\nThe Developer grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, free right to use the App on your devices for personal, non-commercial purposes. All rights in the App, its name, icon and texts belong to the Developer. You may not copy or distribute the App outside the app store, present it as your own, or decompile or modify it, except where the law expressly allows.\n\n3. "As is"\nThe App helps you make shopping lists. It is provided "as is" and "as available". The Developer does not guarantee that it will work without interruption or errors, suit your purposes, or that reminders will fire exactly on time (this depends on your phone\'s battery and notification settings).\n\n4. Your data and backups\nAll data is stored only on your phone. You are responsible for its content and safekeeping. We recommend saving a backup regularly ("Settings" → "Backup") and keeping it somewhere safe. Data may be lost if you uninstall the App, reset or lose your phone.\n\n5. Prices, totals and budget\nAmounts, prices, budgets and totals are for information only; they are calculated from what you enter and are not financial, tax or other advice. The product catalogue and suggestions are examples; they do not guarantee that prices or availability are accurate or current.\n\n6. Acceptable use\nYou agree not to use the App for unlawful purposes or in a way that infringes the rights of others. The content of lists you send to other people is your responsibility.\n\n7. Limitation of liability\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, the Developer is not liable for indirect loss, lost profit or loss of data arising from use of, or inability to use, the App, and the Developer\'s total liability will not exceed the amount you paid for the App (the App is free). This does not limit rights that cannot be limited by law (including consumer rights) or liability for intentional misconduct.\n\n8. Changes and termination\nThe Developer may update the App and these terms; for material changes the new version will be shown in the App and continued use means you accept it. You may stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it. The Developer may end support or distribution of the App.\n\n9. Governing law\nThese terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kazakhstan. The parties will try to resolve disputes by negotiation and otherwise as provided by law. If a provision is invalid, the rest remains in force. If you are a consumer, mandatory consumer-protection rules of your country continue to apply.\n\n10. Contact\nquiteusefulapp · quiteusefulapp@gmail.com',
    'terms.privacyBody': 'Effective 13 November 2026 · Version 1.0\n\n1. Summary\nSmart Shopping List (also named "Умный список покупок" and "Smart Tizim" in some languages; the "App") runs on your phone. It has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no server of its own. The Developer does not collect, receive, store, sell or share your personal data.\n\n2. What data is in the App and where it lives\nEverything you enter (lists, items, quantities, prices, budgets, dishes, purchase history, dates and reminders, settings) is stored only on your device, in the App\'s own database. The Developer has no access to it.\nIt is deleted when you uninstall the App or clear its data in Android settings (Settings → Apps → the App → Storage → Clear data). Backup files you saved yourself must be deleted by you.\n\n3. Permissions and why\n• Notifications and exact alarms — to show the shopping reminders you set, at the time you choose. Reminders are created and run on the device; nothing is sent anywhere.\n• Microphone / speech recognition (only when you tap the voice-input button) — to turn speech into item text. Recognition is performed by your phone\'s speech-recognition service, which on many devices is provided by Google and depends on your Android settings. That service is separate from the Developer and is governed by its own terms and privacy policy. The Developer does not receive the audio or the recognized text. Voice input is optional; every feature works with the keyboard.\nThe App does not request access to contacts, location, camera, photos, files, accounts, SMS or calls.\n\n4. Internet\nThe Google Play version of the App does not send data over the internet and contains no advertising or analytics libraries. The only exceptions are the external speech-recognition service (section 3) if you use it, and links you open in your browser yourself.\n\n5. Sharing\nThe Developer shares nothing with third parties. Data leaves your device only when you act: when you tap "Share" or "Save backup", or send a list file or text through an app you choose (messenger, email, cloud). From then on, that app is responsible.\n\n6. Children\nThe App is not directed at children and collects no data from anyone, including children. If you believe a child has sent data to the Developer, write to the address above.\n\n7. Security\nData is kept in the App\'s protected storage on your device; device security (screen lock, Android updates, backups) is up to you. A backup file you save is not encrypted — store and send it with care.\n\n8. Your rights\nBecause the Developer does not process your personal data, there is nothing to access, correct or delete on the Developer\'s side: you control your data yourself (edit and delete lists, clear the App\'s data). If you believe the Developer has nevertheless received your data, write to the address above — we will reply within a reasonable time (up to 30 days), tell you what we hold and delete it on request. You may also contact the data-protection authority in your country. This policy follows the general principles of the Law of the Republic of Kazakhstan "On Personal Data and Their Protection" (No. 94-V of 21 May 2013) and of the GDPR (data minimisation, transparency, on-device storage).\n\n9. Changes\nIf this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page and shown in the App, and the date above will change. A new App version will not start collecting data without a separate clear notice and your consent.\n\n10. Contact\nquiteusefulapp · quiteusefulapp@gmail.com',
